#'   your starting tick (e.g. to set the starting tick to 100, set the
#'   `tick0` to 2) except when `dtick`="L<f>" (see `dtick` for more info).
#'   If the axis `type` is "date", it should be a date string, like date
#'   data. If the axis `type` is "category", it should be a number, using
#'   the scale where each category is assigned a serial number from zero in
#'   the order it appears. Any value.
#' @param tickangle Sets the angle of the tick labels with respect to the
#'   horizontal. For example, a `tickangle` of -90 draws the tick labels
#'   vertically. Angle in degrees.
#' @param tickcolor Sets the tick color. Color: a CSS color string or R
#'   color name.
#' @param tickfont Sets the color bar's tick label font Named list or
#'   \code{\link{go_scattergl_marker_colorbar_tickfont}()} object.
#' @param tickformat Sets the tick label formatting rule using d3
#'   formatting mini-languages which are very similar to those in Python.
#'   For numbers, see:
#'   https://github.com/d3/d3-format/tree/v1.4.5#d3-format. And for dates
#'   see: https://github.com/d3/d3-time-format/tree/v2.2.3#locale_format.
#'   We add two items to d3's date formatter: "\%h" for half of the year as
#'   a decimal number as well as "\%\{n\}f" for fractional seconds with n
#'   digits. For example, "2016-10-13 09:15:23.456" with tickformat
#'   "\%H~\%M~\%S.\%2f" would display "09~15~23.46" String.
#' @param tickformatstops List of named lists or
#'   \code{\link{go_scattergl_marker_colorbar_tickformatstop}()} objects.
#' @param ticklabeloverflow Determines how we handle tick labels that would
#'   overflow either the graph div or the domain of the axis. The default
#'   value for inside tick labels is "hide past domain". In other cases the
#'   default is "hide past div". One of \code{"allow"}, \code{"hide past
#'   div"}, \code{"hide past domain"}.
#' @param ticklabelposition Determines where tick labels are drawn relative
#'   to the ticks. Left and right options are used when `orientation` is
#'   "h", top and bottom when `orientation` is "v". One of
#'   \code{"outside"}, \code{"inside"}, \code{"outside top"}, \code{"inside
#'   top"}, \code{"outside left"}, \code{"inside left"}, \code{"outside
#'   right"}, \code{"inside right"}, \code{"outside bottom"}, \code{"inside
#'   bottom"}.
#' @param ticklabelstep Sets the spacing between tick labels as compared to
#'   the spacing between ticks. A value of 1 (default) means each tick gets
#'   a label. A value of 2 means shows every 2nd label. A larger value n
#'   means only every nth tick is labeled. `tick0` determines which labels
#'   are shown. Not implemented for axes with `type` "log" or
#'   "multicategory", or when `tickmode` is "array". Integer in the
#'   interval [1, Inf].
#' @param ticklen Sets the tick length (in px). Number in the interval [0,
#'   Inf].
#' @param tickmode Sets the tick mode for this axis. If "auto", the number
#'   of ticks is set via `nticks`. If "linear", the placement of the ticks
#'   is determined by a starting position `tick0` and a tick step `dtick`
#'   ("linear" is the default value if `tick0` and `dtick` are provided).
#'   If "array", the placement of the ticks is set via `tickvals` and the
#'   tick text is `ticktext`. ("array" is the default value if `tickvals`
#'   is provided). One of \code{"auto"}, \code{"linear"}, \code{"array"}.
#' @param tickprefix Sets a tick label prefix. String.
#' @param ticks Determines whether ticks are drawn or not. If **, this
#'   axis' ticks are not drawn. If "outside" ("inside"), this axis' are
#'   drawn outside (inside) the axis lines. One of \code{"outside"},
#'   \code{"inside"}, \code{""}.
#' @param ticksuffix Sets a tick label suffix. String.
#' @param ticktext Sets the text displayed at the ticks position via
#'   `tickvals`. Only has an effect if `tickmode` is set to "array". Used
#'   with `tickvals`. Data array: a vector, factor, Date/POSIXct vector,
#'   matrix or list.
#' @param tickvals Sets the values at which ticks on this axis appear. Only
#'   has an effect if `tickmode` is set to "array". Used with `ticktext`.
#'   Data array: a vector, factor, Date/POSIXct vector, matrix or list.
#' @param tickwidth Sets the tick width (in px). Number in the interval [0,
#'   Inf].
#' @param title String (the title text), named list or
#'   \code{\link{go_scattergl_marker_colorbar_title}()} object.
#' @param traceref Integer in the interval [0, Inf].
#' @param tracerefminus Integer in the interval [0, Inf].
#' @param type Determines the rule used to generate the error bars. If
#'   "constant", the bar lengths are of a constant value. Set this constant
#'   in `value`. If "percent", the bar lengths correspond to a percentage
#'   of underlying data. Set this percentage in `value`. If "sqrt", the bar
#'   lengths correspond to the square of the underlying data. If "data",
#'   the bar lengths are set with data set `array`. One of
#'   \code{"percent"}, \code{"constant"}, \code{"sqrt"}, \code{"data"}.
#' @param uid Assign an id to this trace, Use this to provide object
#'   constancy between traces during animations and transitions. String.
#' @param uirevision Controls persistence of some user-driven changes to
#'   the trace: `constraintrange` in `parcoords` traces, as well as some
#'   `editable: true` modifications such as `name` and `colorbar.title`.
#'   Defaults to `layout.uirevision`. Note that other user-driven trace
#'   attribute changes are controlled by `layout` attributes:
#'   `trace.visible` is controlled by `layout.legend.uirevision`,
#'   `selectedpoints` is controlled by `layout.selectionrevision`, and
#'   `colorbar.(x|y)` (accessible with `config: \{editable: true\}`) is
#'   controlled by `layout.editrevision`. Trace changes are tracked by
#'   `uid`, which only falls back on trace index if no `uid` is provided.
#'   So if your app can add/remove traces before the end of the `data`
#'   array, such that the same trace has a different index, you can still
#'   preserve user-driven changes if you give each trace a `uid` that stays
#'   with it as it moves. Any value.
#' @param unselected Named list or \code{\link{go_scattergl_unselected}()}
#'   object.
#' @param value \strong{\code{go_scattergl_error_x()},
#'   \code{go_scattergl_error_y()}}: Sets the value of either the
#'   percentage (if `type` is set to "percent") or the constant (if `type`
#'   is set to "constant") corresponding to the lengths of the error bars.
#'   Number in the interval [0, Inf].
#'
#'   \strong{\code{go_scattergl_marker_colorbar_tickformatstop()}}: string
#'   - dtickformat for described zoom level, the same as "tickformat"
#'   String.
#' @param valueminus Sets the value of either the percentage (if `type` is
#'   set to "percent") or the constant (if `type` is set to "constant")
#'   corresponding to the lengths of the error bars in the bottom (left)
#'   direction for vertical (horizontal) bars Number in the interval [0,
#'   Inf].
#' @param variant \strong{\code{go_scattergl_hoverlabel_font()}}: Sets the
#'   variant of the font. One of \code{"normal"}, \code{"small-caps"},
#'   \code{"all-small-caps"}, \code{"all-petite-caps"},
#'   \code{"petite-caps"}, \code{"unicase"}, or a vector of these.
#'
#'   \strong{\code{go_scattergl_legendgrouptitle_font()},
#'   \code{go_scattergl_marker_colorbar_tickfont()},
#'   \code{go_scattergl_marker_colorbar_title_font()}}: Sets the variant of
#'   the font. One of \code{"normal"}, \code{"small-caps"},
#'   \code{"all-small-caps"}, \code{"all-petite-caps"},
#'   \code{"petite-caps"}, \code{"unicase"}.
#'
#'   \strong{\code{go_scattergl_textfont()}}: Sets the variant of the font.
#'   One of \code{"normal"}, \code{"small-caps"}, or a vector of these.
#' @param visible \strong{\code{go_scattergl()}}: Determines whether or not
#'   this trace is visible. If "legendonly", the trace is not drawn, but
#'   can appear as a legend item (provided that the legend itself is
#'   visible). One of \code{"legendonly"}, \code{TRUE}, \code{FALSE}.
#'
#'   \strong{\code{go_scattergl_error_x()}, \code{go_scattergl_error_y()}}:
#'   Determines whether or not this set of error bars is visible. Logical.
#' @param weight \strong{\code{go_scattergl_hoverlabel_font()}}: Sets the
#'   weight (or boldness) of the font. Integer in the interval [1, 1000],
#'   or a vector of these.
#'
#'   \strong{\code{go_scattergl_legendgrouptitle_font()},
#'   \code{go_scattergl_marker_colorbar_tickfont()},
#'   \code{go_scattergl_marker_colorbar_title_font()}}: Sets the weight (or
#'   boldness) of the font. Integer in the interval [1, 1000].
#'
#'   \strong{\code{go_scattergl_textfont()}}: Sets the weight (or boldness)
#'   of the font. One of \code{"normal"}, \code{"bold"}, or a vector of
#'   these.
#' @param width \strong{\code{go_scattergl_error_x()},
#'   \code{go_scattergl_error_y()}}: Sets the width (in px) of the
#'   cross-bar at both ends of the error bars. Number in the interval [0,
#'   Inf].
#'
#'   \strong{\code{go_scattergl_line()}}: Sets the line width (in px).
#'   Number in the interval [0, Inf].
#'
#'   \strong{\code{go_scattergl_marker_line()}}: Sets the width (in px) of
#'   the lines bounding the marker points. Number in the interval [0, Inf],
#'   or a vector of these.
#' @param x \strong{\code{go_scattergl()}}: Sets the x coordinates. Data
#'   array: a vector, factor, Date/POSIXct vector, matrix or list.
#'
#'   \strong{\code{go_scattergl_marker_colorbar()}}: Sets the x position
#'   with respect to `xref` of the color bar (in plot fraction). When
#'   `xref` is "paper", defaults to 1.02 when `orientation` is "v" and 0.5
#'   when `orientation` is "h". When `xref` is "container", defaults to 1
#'   when `orientation` is "v" and 0.5 when `orientation` is "h". Must be
#'   between 0 and 1 if `xref` is "container" and between "-2" and 3 if
#'   `xref` is "paper". Number.
#' @param x0 Alternate to `x`. Builds a linear space of x coordinates. Use
#'   with `dx` where `x0` is the starting coordinate and `dx` the step. Any
#'   value.
#' @param xanchor Sets this color bar's horizontal position anchor. This
#'   anchor binds the `x` position to the "left", "center" or "right" of
#'   the color bar. Defaults to "left" when `orientation` is "v" and
#'   "center" when `orientation` is "h". One of \code{"left"},
#'   \code{"center"}, \code{"right"}.
#' @param xaxis Sets a reference between this trace's x coordinates and a
#'   2D cartesian x axis. If "x" (the default value), the x coordinates
#'   refer to `layout.xaxis`. If "x2", the x coordinates refer to
#'   `layout.xaxis2`, and so on. Subplot id: \code{"x"}, \code{"x2"},
#'   \code{"x3"}, ....
#' @param xcalendar Sets the calendar system to use with `x` date data. One
#'   of \code{"chinese"}, \code{"coptic"}, \code{"discworld"},
#'   \code{"ethiopian"}, \code{"gregorian"}, \code{"hebrew"},
#'   \code{"islamic"}, \code{"jalali"}, \code{"julian"}, \code{"mayan"},
#'   \code{"nanakshahi"}, \code{"nepali"}, \code{"persian"},
#'   \code{"taiwan"}, \code{"thai"}, \code{"ummalqura"}.
#' @param xhoverformat Sets the hover text formatting rule for `x` using d3
#'   formatting mini-languages which are very similar to those in Python.
#'   For numbers, see:
#'   https://github.com/d3/d3-format/tree/v1.4.5#d3-format. And for dates
#'   see: https://github.com/d3/d3-time-format/tree/v2.2.3#locale_format.
#'   We add two items to d3's date formatter: "\%h" for half of the year as
#'   a decimal number as well as "\%\{n\}f" for fractional seconds with n
#'   digits. For example, "2016-10-13 09:15:23.456" with tickformat
#'   "\%H~\%M~\%S.\%2f" would display "09~15~23.46"By default the values
#'   are formatted using `xaxis.hoverformat`. String.
#' @param xpad Sets the amount of padding (in px) along the x direction.
#'   Number in the interval [0, Inf].
#' @param xperiod Only relevant when the axis `type` is "date". Sets the
#'   period positioning in milliseconds or "M<n>" on the x axis. Special
#'   values in the form of "M<n>" could be used to declare the number of
#'   months. In this case `n` must be a positive integer. Any value.
#' @param xperiod0 Only relevant when the axis `type` is "date". Sets the
#'   base for period positioning in milliseconds or date string on the x0
#'   axis. When `x0period` is round number of weeks, the `x0period0` by
#'   default would be on a Sunday i.e. 2000-01-02, otherwise it would be at
#'   2000-01-01. Any value.
#' @param xperiodalignment Only relevant when the axis `type` is "date".
#'   Sets the alignment of data points on the x axis. One of
#'   \code{"start"}, \code{"middle"}, \code{"end"}.
#' @param xref Sets the container `x` refers to. "container" spans the
#'   entire `width` of the plot. "paper" refers to the width of the
#'   plotting area only. One of \code{"container"}, \code{"paper"}.
#' @param y \strong{\code{go_scattergl()}}: Sets the y coordinates. Data
#'   array: a vector, factor, Date/POSIXct vector, matrix or list.
#'
#'   \strong{\code{go_scattergl_marker_colorbar()}}: Sets the y position
#'   with respect to `yref` of the color bar (in plot fraction). When
#'   `yref` is "paper", defaults to 0.5 when `orientation` is "v" and 1.02
#'   when `orientation` is "h". When `yref` is "container", defaults to 0.5
#'   when `orientation` is "v" and 1 when `orientation` is "h". Must be
#'   between 0 and 1 if `yref` is "container" and between "-2" and 3 if
#'   `yref` is "paper". Number.
#' @param y0 Alternate to `y`. Builds a linear space of y coordinates. Use
#'   with `dy` where `y0` is the starting coordinate and `dy` the step. Any
#'   value.
#' @param yanchor Sets this color bar's vertical position anchor This
#'   anchor binds the `y` position to the "top", "middle" or "bottom" of
#'   the color bar. Defaults to "middle" when `orientation` is "v" and
#'   "bottom" when `orientation` is "h". One of \code{"top"},
#'   \code{"middle"}, \code{"bottom"}.
#' @param yaxis Sets a reference between this trace's y coordinates and a
#'   2D cartesian y axis. If "y" (the default value), the y coordinates
#'   refer to `layout.yaxis`. If "y2", the y coordinates refer to
#'   `layout.yaxis2`, and so on. Subplot id: \code{"y"}, \code{"y2"},
#'   \code{"y3"}, ....
#' @param ycalendar Sets the calendar system to use with `y` date data. One
#'   of \code{"chinese"}, \code{"coptic"}, \code{"discworld"},
#'   \code{"ethiopian"}, \code{"gregorian"}, \code{"hebrew"},
#'   \code{"islamic"}, \code{"jalali"}, \code{"julian"}, \code{"mayan"},
#'   \code{"nanakshahi"}, \code{"nepali"}, \code{"persian"},
#'   \code{"taiwan"}, \code{"thai"}, \code{"ummalqura"}.
#' @param yhoverformat Sets the hover text formatting rule for `y` using d3
#'   formatting mini-languages which are very similar to those in Python.
#'   For numbers, see:
#'   https://github.com/d3/d3-format/tree/v1.4.5#d3-format. And for dates
#'   see: https://github.com/d3/d3-time-format/tree/v2.2.3#locale_format.
#'   We add two items to d3's date formatter: "\%h" for half of the year as
#'   a decimal number as well as "\%\{n\}f" for fractional seconds with n
#'   digits. For example, "2016-10-13 09:15:23.456" with tickformat
#'   "\%H~\%M~\%S.\%2f" would display "09~15~23.46"By default the values
#'   are formatted using `yaxis.hoverformat`. String.
#' @param ypad Sets the amount of padding (in px) along the y direction.
#'   Number in the interval [0, Inf].
#' @param yperiod Only relevant when the axis `type` is "date". Sets the
#'   period positioning in milliseconds or "M<n>" on the y axis. Special
#'   values in the form of "M<n>" could be used to declare the number of
#'   months. In this case `n` must be a positive integer. Any value.
#' @param yperiod0 Only relevant when the axis `type` is "date". Sets the
#'   base for period positioning in milliseconds or date string on the y0
#'   axis. When `y0period` is round number of weeks, the `y0period0` by
#'   default would be on a Sunday i.e. 2000-01-02, otherwise it would be at
#'   2000-01-01. Any value.
#' @param yperiodalignment Only relevant when the axis `type` is "date".
#'   Sets the alignment of data points on the y axis. One of
#'   \code{"start"}, \code{"middle"}, \code{"end"}.
#' @param yref Sets the container `y` refers to. "container" spans the
#'   entire `height` of the plot. "paper" refers to the height of the
#'   plotting area only. One of \code{"container"}, \code{"paper"}.
#' @param ... Further properties, including nested properties in
#'   "magic underscore" form, e.g. \code{marker_size = 10} for
#'   \code{marker = list(size = 10)}. Property values may be one-sided
#'   formulas, evaluated in \code{data} for \code{add_*()} functions.
#' @param skip_invalid If \code{TRUE}, silently drop invalid properties
#'   instead of raising an error.
#' @return Each \code{go_*()} function returns a graph object of the same
#'   class as its name; \code{add_*()} functions return the modified figure.
#' @seealso \code{\link{go_figure}()}, \code{\link{add_trace}()}
#' @noMd
#' @export
#' @examples
#' go_scattergl(x = 1:3, y = c(2, 1, 3), mode = "markers", marker_color = "red")
go_scattergl <- function(
    arg = NULL, ..., connectgaps = NULL, customdata = NULL, dx = NULL,
    dy = NULL, error_x = NULL, error_y = NULL, fill = NULL,
    fillcolor = NULL, hoverinfo = NULL, hoverlabel = NULL,
    hovertemplate = NULL, hovertemplatefallback = NULL, hovertext = NULL,
    ids = NULL, legend = NULL, legendgroup = NULL, legendgrouptitle = NULL,
    legendrank = NULL, legendwidth = NULL, line = NULL, marker = NULL,
    meta = NULL, mode = NULL, name = NULL, opacity = NULL, selected = NULL,
    selectedpoints = NULL, showlegend = NULL, text = NULL, textfont = NULL,
    textposition = NULL, texttemplate = NULL, texttemplatefallback = NULL,
    uid = NULL, uirevision = NULL, unselected = NULL, visible = NULL,
    x = NULL, x0 = NULL, xaxis = NULL, xcalendar = NULL,
    xhoverformat = NULL, xperiod = NULL, xperiod0 = NULL,
    xperiodalignment = NULL, y = NULL, y0 = NULL, yaxis = NULL,
    ycalendar = NULL, yhoverformat = NULL, yperiod = NULL, yperiod0 = NULL,
    yperiodalignment = NULL, skip_invalid = FALSE
) {
  plotly_object("scattergl", arg, environment(), list(...), skip_invalid)
}

